<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-polar-coordinates" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

    <title>Polar Coordinates</title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            In this section, we will learn a completely different way of organizing the coordinate 
            plane: polar coordinates, where a polar point, <m>(\rho,\theta)</m>, has a radius <m>\rho</m>
            from the origin and the angle from standard position, <m>\theta</m>. We will practice 
            plotting points using polar coordinates, converting between polar coordinates and 
            rectangular coordinates, transforming equations between polar and rectangular forms, and 
            graphing polar equations.
        </p>
    </introduction>

    <subsection>
        <title>Textbook Reference</title>
        <p> 
            This relates to content in <section-mark/>10.3 and <section-mark/>10.4 of
            <url href="https://openstax.org/details/books/algebra-and-trigonometry-2e" visual="http://tiny.cc/111Z-Textbook">Algebra and Trigonometry 2e</url>.
        </p>
    </subsection>

